      {
        "id": "p79-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Identify the mode of each dataset. Explain one limitation of using the mode as a measure of centre here.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p79-q2-a-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Both modes are ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "8",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". This is the smallest and most frequent value, while the middle observation is 9. The mode does not describe the position of all the data.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "In each dataset, 8 occurs twice and every other value occurs once. Both modes are $8$.\n\nThe mode describes the most frequent value, but the middle observation in each dataset is 9. It does not describe the position of all the observations. It remains useful when the most common value is the feature of interest.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p79-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the mean of each of the sets of scores.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p79-q2-b-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Dataset 1: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "9.2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; Dataset 2: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "29",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Dataset 1:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\bar{x}_1&=\\frac{8+8+9+10+11}{5}\\\\\\bar{x}_1&=\\frac{46}{5}\\\\\\bar{x}_1&=9.2\\end{align*}$$\n\nDataset 2:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\bar{x}_2&=\\frac{8+8+9+10+110}{5}\\\\\\bar{x}_2&=\\frac{145}{5}\\\\\\bar{x}_2&=29\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p79-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Explain why the mean is a good measure of centre for the first dataset, but not the second.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p79-q2-c-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "9.2 represents Dataset 1's cluster from 8 to 11. In Dataset 2, the outlier 110 pulls the mean up to 29, away from the other values from 8 to 10.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Dataset 1's values lie from 8 to 11, and its mean of 9.2 represents that cluster.\n\nDataset 2 has four values from 8 to 10 and an outlier of 110. Because the mean uses every value, 110 raises the mean to 29, well above the main cluster.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p79-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Would the median or mode be a better measure of centre for dataset 2?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p79-q2-d-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The median, ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "9",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", represents the middle observation in the main cluster without being pulled upward by 110.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Ordered values: $8, 8, 9, 10, 110$.\n\nThe third of the five values is 9, so the median is $9$. The mode is $8$.\n\nThe median is the better choice for describing the middle of the main cluster. The extreme value 110 does not pull this middle value upward.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      }
    ]
